508	\subsection{DFT registers}
509	\label{dft}
510	In addition to the single bin DFT configured through the ADC prescaler and phase increment registers (see \ref{reg:ADC} and \ref{reg:phaseinc}), the FPGA also includes a multiple point DFT. This DFT only operates on the port 1 and port 2 receivers and is intended to speed up spectrum analyzer measurements. If enabled, the DFT runs in parallel to all other calculations.
511	
512	The DFT has a fixed number of bins (96), but the frequencies these bins correspond to can be changed.
513	
514	\subsubsection{DFT\_FIRST\_BIN: 0x12}
515	\begin{center}
516	\begin{tikzpicture}
517	\bitrect{16}{16-\bit}
518	\rwbits{0}{16}{DFT\_FIRST\_BIN[15:0]}
519	\end{tikzpicture}
520	\end{center}
521	\begin{itemize}
522	\item \textbf{DFT\_FIRST\_BIN[15:0]:} This value determines the frequency corresponding to the first DFT bin.
523	$$ f_{firstBin} =  \frac{SR_{ADC} * DFT\_FIRST\_BIN}{2^{16}}$$
524	\end{itemize}
525	
526	\subsubsection{DFT\_FREQ\_SPACING: 0x13}
527	\begin{center}
528	\begin{tikzpicture}
529	\bitrect{16}{16-\bit}
530	\rwbits{0}{16}{DFT\_FREQ\_SPACING[15:0]}
531	\end{tikzpicture}
532	\end{center}
533	\begin{itemize}
534	\item \textbf{DFT\_FREQ\_SPACING[15:0]:} This value determines the frequency difference between bins.
535	$$ \Delta f =  \frac{SR_{ADC} * DFT\_FREQ\_SPACING}{2^{24}}$$
536	\end{itemize}
537	
538	\subsection{SETTLING\_TIME: 0x14}
539	\begin{center}
540	\begin{tikzpicture}
541	\bitrect{16}{16-\bit}
